  "releaseNotes": "Search settings a dataset can choose for itself, on Indx server.\n      \n      - Changed: **a search sent over HTTP can leave coverage settings out.** `QueryProxy.CoverageDepth`\n        is now an `int?`, and `QueryProxy.CoverageSetup` is a `CoverageSetupProxy`, the same settings\n        with every one optional. A setting left out is taken from the dataset's query parameters on\n        the server, and where the dataset sets none, from the usual default. A setting you send always\n        wins. The JSON a search sends is unchanged. In C#, build the settings with\n        `new CoverageSetupProxy { IncludePatternMatches = false }` where you wrote `new CoverageSetup`,\n        and set only what the search needs to decide. `SearchEngine`, `Query` and `CoverageSetup` are\n        unchanged.\n      - Added: **the package carries the licences of the open-source code inside it.** Vector search\n        is built on a port of FAISS (MIT) and hnswlib (Apache 2.0); `THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md` and the\n        `ThirdParty` folder now ship in the package, and the licence says how they apply. 5.0.2 left\n        them out.",
  "requireLicenseAcceptance": true,
  "title": "IndxSearchLib",
  "verbatimVersion": "5.0.3",
